    "definite integrals"
  ],
  "data": {
    "integrand": "2x (x^2 + 1)^3",
    "lower": "0",
    "upper": "1"
  },
  "answer": "15/4",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "With u = x² + 1, what are u's values when x = 0 and x = 1?"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Let $u = x^2 + 1$, $du = 2x\\,dx$. When $x = 0$, $u = 1$; when $x = 1$, $u = 2$.",
    "$\\int_1^2 u^3\\,du = \\left[\\tfrac{u^4}{4}\\right]_1^2 = 4 - \\tfrac14 = \\tfrac{15}{4}$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc2",
    "section": "1.5 Substitution",
    "note": "Original problem; see substitution with definite integrals."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
